# How GitHub should read this repository.
#
# GitHub detects languages, not frameworks: there is no "Angular" for it to
# find, and there never will be. What it can get right is which files are
# written by a person and which are produced by a tool, and by default it
# counts both. That skews the language bar and buries real changes under
# generated ones in every diff.
#
# `linguist-generated` does two things: keeps the file out of the language
# statistics, and collapses it in pull requests. Both are what you want for a
# file whose only correct edit is to regenerate it.

# The contract. Produced by api/tools/dump_openapi.py and generate_dtos.py from
# the response models, and checked by tests that fail if either is stale. Its
# header says as much; a hand edit here is a lie about what the server sends.
web/src/app/core/contract/openapi.json linguist-generated=true
web/src/app/core/contract/dto.ts       linguist-generated=true

# npm's resolution of the dependency tree. Committed on purpose so a build is
# reproducible, but nobody writes it.
web/package-lock.json                  linguist-generated=true

# Normalise line endings so a file written on Windows and one written by a tool
# do not show up as wholly rewritten. Git already warns about this on nearly
# every commit here.
* text=auto
